{"strongs": "H3499", "word": "יֶ֫תֶר", "translit": "ye.ter", "root": "יתן", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "remainder, excellence, excess", "definition": "I. יֶ֫תֶר 94 noun masculine Neh 2:16 remainder, excellence, excess ; — absolute יֶ֫תֶר Neh 2:16 + 2 t.; יָ֑תֶר Prov 17:7 construct יֶ֫תֶר Gen 49:3 + 84 t.; יֶ֫תֶר Isa 56:12 (see Baer's note); suffix יִתְרוֺ Isa 44:19 יִתְרָם Exod 23:11 + 2 t. (not Job 4:21 , q. v. below II. יֶתֶר ); — 1. \\ \\ a. remainder, remnant (with implied inferiority in number or quality), of crops, etc. יִתְרָם Exod 23:11 ( J E ), their remnant , i.e. what they (the enemy) leave, so יֶתֶר הַגָּזָם Joel 1:4 יֶתֶר הָאַרְבֶּה v Joel 1:4 יֶתֶר הַיֶּלֶק v Joel 1:4 יֶתֶר הַפְּלֵטָה הַנִּשְׁאֶרֶת Exod 10:5 ( J ); of vessels, יֶתֶר הַכֵּלִים הַנּוֺתָרִים Jer 27:19 of a tree Isa 44:19 (= שְׁאֵרִית v Isa 44:17 ); elsewhere of person Deut 3:11 = Josh 12:4 ; Josh 3:12 (both D ), Deut 28:54 ; Josh 23:12 ( D ), 2Sam 21:2 ; 2Kgs 25:11 = Jer 52:15 ; Ezek 34:18 of a rescued remnant of Israel (Judah) Mic 5:2 ; Zeph 2:9 (|| שְׁאֵרִית ), Zech 14:2 יֶתֶר הַקָּדֵשׁ אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁאַר 1Kgs 22:47 יֶתֶר הָעָם הַנִּשְׁאָרִים Jer 36:9 (twice in verse); 2Kgs 25:11 = Jer 52:15 . \\ \\ b. remainder, rest, other part of people, elders, etc., 2Sam 10:10 = 1Chr 19:11 ; 2Sam 12:28 ; 1Kgs 12:23 ; Jer 29:1 ; Hab 2:8 ; Ezek 48:23 sometimes including a majority Judg 7:6 ; 1Sam 13:2 of common people (opposed to rulers) Neh 2:16 ; Neh 4:8 ; Neh 4:13 compare Neh 6:1 of land Deut 3:13 ; Josh 13:27 ( P ); of other inanimate things Lev 14:17 ( P ), Num 31:32 ( id. ), of years Isa 38:10 elsewhere in phrase יֶחֶר דִּבְרֵי the rest of the affairs of , in summaries of reigns of kings of Israel and Judah 1Kgs 11:41 + 41 t. Kings Chronicles; יֶתֶר כָּלדִּֿבְרֵי 1Kgs 15:23 יֶתֶר דְּבָרָיו 2Chr 28:26 . 2. a. excess , שְׂפַת יָ֑תֶר Prov 17:7 a lip of excess = arrogant speech (see VB ). \\ \\ b. in adverb phrases, עַל יֶתֶר Ps 31:24 on the basis of abundance = abundantly , as adverb accusative גָּדוֺל יֶתֶר מְאֹד Isa 56:12 great, in abundance , exceedingly, Dan 8:9 וַתִּגְדַּליֶֿתֶר and grew great in excess, exceedingly (compare much , more than ). \\ \\ c. specifically what is over and above immediate necessities, abundance, affluence Job 22:20 ; Ps 17:14 . 3. superiority, excellency יֶתֶר שְׂאֵת וְיֶתֶר עָ֫ז Gen 49:3 . — On Job 4:1 see II. יֶתֶר .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3852')\">BDB3852</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3499')\">H3499</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3851')\">BDB3851</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3853')\">BDB3853</entry></div><p> I. <bdbheb>יֶ֫תֶר</bdbheb><sub>94</sub> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Neh 2:16\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(16,2,16)\">Neh 2:16</ref></sup> <highlightword>remainder, excellence, excess</highlightword>; — absolute <bdbheb>יֶ֫תֶר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Neh 2:16\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(16,2,16)\">Neh 2:16</ref> + 2 t.; <bdbheb>יָ֑תֶר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Prov 17:7\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(20,17,7)\">Prov 17:7</ref> construct <bdbheb>יֶ֫תֶר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 49:3\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"49\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"49\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(1,49,3)\">Gen 49:3</ref> + 84 t.; <bdbheb>יֶ֫תֶר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 56:12\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"56\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"56\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(23,56,12)\">Isa 56:12</ref> (see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Baer')\">Baer's</lookup> note); suffix <bdbheb>יִתְרוֺ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 44:19\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(23,44,19)\">Isa 44:19</ref> <bdbheb>יִתְרָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 23:11\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(2,23,11)\">Exod 23:11</ref> + 2 t. (not <ref ref=\"Job 4:21\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"4\